{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank","id":1280708,"title":"Death Rank","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-14T10:58:52-08:00","id":1280708,"title":"Death Rank","content":"Hello is was wondering in regards to having 4 in Spirit and I gain attainment: Honorary Rank , if I have 4 in Death does that apply to ghosts. From what I read ghosts have ranks as well and would I get the same social bonus with them? Mind 4 and Goetia as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8204-nocturnas","name":"Nocturnas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T11:24:33-08:00","id":1280711,"title":"","content":"Not without an alternative Attainment to that effect, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:59:56-08:00","id":1280732,"title":"","content":"How much do the attainments cost to purchase, anyone know?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8204-nocturnas","name":"Nocturnas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T13:02:39-08:00","id":1280733,"title":"","content":"Im guessing the same as a legacy , since only legacy is mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8204-nocturnas","name":"Nocturnas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T13:25:23-08:00","id":1280737,"title":"","content":"Based on the following I think you get them for free when you buy a relevant Arcanum dot. You'll just have to ask your GM to approve the trade of one Attainment for another. I think they ought to - it's reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.192</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attainments are available to all mages as their understanding of magic (as measured by the Arcana) increases.<br /> As a mage\u2019s rating in an Arcanum increases, she gains access to new Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 01-14-2019, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T13:58:26-08:00","id":1280744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280737#post1280737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the following I think you get them for free when you buy a relevant Arcanum dot. You'll just have to ask your GM to approve the trade of one Attainment for another. I think they ought to - it's reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>At second and fourth dots (the Lesser and Greater Utility Attainments) you can develop other Attainments instead of those written in the book. They're just the most common examples. Since Attainments are taught by the Orders and aren't limited to a set list, many think it should be possible to learn additional Lesser and Greater Utility Attainments, which would require an XP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:02:13-08:00","id":1280747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280744#post1280744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At second and fourth dots (the Lesser and Greater Utility Attainments) you can develop other Attainments instead of those written in the book. They're just the most common examples. Since Attainments are taught by the Orders and aren't limited to a set list, many think it should be possible to learn additional Lesser and Greater Utility Attainments, which would require an XP cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. Non-Legacy Attainements come in as a result of developing the Arcana, and aren't tied into the Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:04:00-08:00","id":1280748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280747#post1280747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Non-Legacy Attainements come in as a result of developing the Arcana, and aren't tied into the Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As a mage\u2019s rating in an Arcanum increases, she gains access<br /> to new Attainments. The Orders instruct their members on<br /> how to use these abilities, but the instruction bears more resemblance to conditioning in athletics or fundamental principles<br /> in mathematics&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:28:12-08:00","id":1280758,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your responses , this has been helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8204-nocturnas","name":"Nocturnas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T06:33:16-08:00","id":1280886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280748#post1280748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;As a mage\u2019s rating in an Arcanum increases, she gains access<br /> to new Attainments. The Orders instruct their members on<br /> how to use these abilities, but the instruction bears more resemblance to conditioning in athletics or fundamental principles<br /> in mathematics&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I had forgotten about that last bit. I still don't think it means you can develop different attainments at different arcana levels, based on the phrasing. I would read it as being similar to High Speech. All awakened have access to it, but if you don't have membership in an Order to spell it out for you then you may have to spend experience to justify the fact that you had to figure it out for yourself . Either way the option is to know High Speech, or not know High Speech - you don't have the option to create an alternative universal awakened meta-what-have-you, and you don't have the option to figure out something other than Sympathetic Range as an attainment at Space 2. And the fact that there is no experience cost listed for attainments does imply to me that the order training thing is mainly just flavor.<br /> That is my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 01-15-2019, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T11:53:43-08:00","id":1280952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280886#post1280886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had forgotten about that last bit. I still don't think it means you can develop different attainments at different arcana levels, based on the phrasing. I would read it as being similar to High Speech. All awakened have access to it, but if you don't have membership in an Order to spell it out for you then you may have to spend experience to justify the fact that you had to figure it out for yourself . Either way the option is to know High Speech, or not know High Speech - you don't have the option to create an alternative universal awakened meta-what-have-you, and you don't have the option to figure out something other than Sympathetic Range as an attainment at Space 2. And the fact that there is no experience cost listed for attainments does imply to me that the order training thing is mainly just flavor.<br /> That is my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was only a reply to Arcane. The texts for the Lesser Utilities quite explicitly state that those are only examples and that people can develop other Attainments. As such it's fully possible for mages with Space 2+ to <i>not</i> have Sympathetic Range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T20:24:19-08:00","id":1281034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1280952#post1280952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was only a reply to Arcane. The texts for the Lesser Utilities quite explicitly state that those are only examples and that people can develop other Attainments. As such it's fully possible for mages with Space 2+ to <i>not</i> have Sympathetic Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang. I guess when I realized I had forgotten about the text regarding the Orders helping train mages on attainments, I just should have reread the entire entry on attainments. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:47:46-08:00","id":1281222,"title":"","content":"I don\u00b4t know about you guys, but here\u00b4s how my Mage ST is running things right now:<br /> -There are many possible Attainments. The ones in the book are simply the best know and the ones that come most intuitively to mages (AKA the ones mages outside of the Orders usually learn). <br /> -A single Mage may have multiple Attainments. So, for example, a single mage may have 3 Lesser Utilities in the same Arcana. This is not common. <br /> -Further Attainments (than the standard ones listed in the corebook) usually require a Mentor or a Grimoire.<br /> -Those fabled Grimoires mages usually kill to get are not usually full of rotes, but instead teach one (or, rarely, more) rare Attainment. One example would be a Grimoire that teaches one how to forge Familiar bonds with Spirits of Rank up to one\u00b4s Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T06:45:08-08:00","id":1281287,"title":"","content":"Nifty. Out of curiosity how does your story teller handle experience if any that must be spent to learn the new attainments? And are there different mage armors too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T11:50:01-08:00","id":1281332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1281287#post1281287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nifty. Out of curiosity how does your story teller handle experience if any that must be spent to learn the new attainments? And are there different mage armors too?</div> </div> </div> </div>It costs 3 per new Attainment. He never mentioned anything about different kinds of Mage Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:19:16-08:00","id":1281554,"title":"","content":"I've always figured that honorary Rank is less important to ghosts, because they tend not to organize into courts, choirs, etc. as spirits of Shadow do.<br /> As for alternate Attainments, I fully plan to replace Matter's 4th-dot attainment with the ability to make Perfected Materials, once Signs of Sorcery comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","user":"Redline","date":". 01-18-2019, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:05:51-08:00","id":1282156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1281554#post1281554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always figured that honorary Rank is less important to ghosts, because they tend not to organize into courts, choirs, etc. as spirits of Shadow do.<br /> As for alternate Attainments, I fully plan to replace Matter's 4th-dot attainment with the ability to make Perfected Materials, once Signs of Sorcery comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that having an honorary Rank for ghosts wouldn't mean much. &quot;Oh you're a higher rank ghost? Good for you.&quot; My understanding of ghosts is they just don't have the social structure present for it to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T12:26:11-08:00","id":1282174,"title":"","content":"Outranking a ghost by two Ranks still inflicts Bane damage, same as spirits. That's pretty significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T13:04:57-08:00","id":1282188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1280708-death-rank?p=1282174#post1282174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outranking a ghost by two Ranks still inflicts Bane damage, same as spirits. That's pretty significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that depends on the individual mage's Brawl skill, and/or willingness to punch or bite a given ghost. I figure that at Death 4 you have better options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}